# Codex Code Review Gate

Before declaring code complete or finalizing file edits:
1. Conduct an adversarial code review checking:
   - Correctness and edge case handling (empty inputs, null pointers, timeouts).
   - Resource leaks (unclosed streams, hanging event listeners).
   - Performance bottlenecks ($O(N^2)$ loops, duplicate queries).
   - Readability, naming, and idiomatic style.
2. Present findings inside:
```text
✦ Codex review: <Topic>
- Correctness: [Pass / Action item]
- Security: [Pass / Action item]
- Robustness: [Pass / Action item]
- Overall Grade: [Production Ready / Revision Needed]
```
